# T0019 — Priority field colors in List View

## Goal

Color the Priority field in task list views so priority is scannable at a glance, using the palette from the task description.

## Decisions (confirmed)

1. Surfaces: global `/tasks` list **and** project TaskBoard list rows.
2. Color the Priority `<select>` text via shared CSS tokens / modifiers (same pattern as T0020 state colors).
3. `none` → default `--text` (no accent), like State “New”.

## Color map

| Priority | Color |
|----------|--------|
| Urgent | Red |
| High | Orange |
| Medium | Yellow |
| Low | Green |
| None | Default text |

Concrete tokens (aligned with existing dark UI accents where sensible):

- `--task-priority-urgent`: `#e55` (match canceled / danger red)
- `--task-priority-high`: `#e8a838` or a clearer orange (e.g. `#f08a3a`)
- `--task-priority-medium`: `#e8c84a` (yellow)
- `--task-priority-low`: `#3ecf8e` or accent green (`#7dd87d` / `#3ecf8e`)

## Approach

1. Add `taskPriorityTone` / `taskPriorityClass` helpers in `client/src/lib/taskFields.ts` (mirror `taskStateTone` / `taskStateClass`).
2. CSS variables on theme `:root` + modifiers:
   - `.task-list-row__priority--urgent|high|medium|low`
3. Apply `taskPriorityClass("task-list-row__priority", task.priority)` on the Priority `<select>` in:
   - `client/src/pages/TasksListPage.tsx`
   - `client/src/components/TaskBoard.tsx` (list row)
4. Ensure the closed select’s text color updates when priority changes (className driven by current value). Dropdown option list can stay native/default.

## Out of scope

- Editor modal Priority select styling (unless trivial reuse).
- Kanban or non-list surfaces.
- Changing priority values or sort order.

## Branch

`T0019-list-priority-color`

## QA checklist (post-implement)

- [ ] Global Tasks: None / Low / Medium / High / Urgent show expected colors on the Priority select.
- [ ] Project task list: same.
- [ ] Changing priority updates color immediately.
- [ ] Select remains usable (click / change works).
- [ ] Readable on dark theme / narrow viewport.
